  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is our best at 0.725 acc, but all tested multimodal multiprofile configs use transformer aggregation. We have no data on whether avgpool aggregation would perform comparably with these same encoders. Question: Does transformer aggregation provide a meaningful accuracy gain over the simpler avgpool, or is it just adding compute cost? This experiment (config_027) is a clean single-variable ablation—identical to config_001 except aggregation changes from transformer to avgpool. Why now: With 5 experiments remaining, resolving whether transformer is necessary frees up budget (avgpool should be ~20-30% cheaper than transformer, estimated ~2.5-3.0 GPU hrs vs 3.60) and clarifies whether we should invest remaining experiments in other axes (RNA encoder, profile setting). If avgpool matches transformer, we save cost; if it falls short, we confirm transformer is essential and can focus exploitation on the remaining untested levers (pca_n2000, singleprofile) without ambiguity."
}

